The {{lang|es|italic=no|[[Apruebo Dignidad]]}} coalition decided its presidential candidate in the publicly-funded primaries held nationwide on 18 July 2021, won by lawmaker [[Gabriel Boric]] with 60% of the vote.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Fuentes|first1=Valentina|last2=Malinowski|first2=Matthew|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-07-18/chile-holds-key-primary-vote-in-wide-open-presidential-race|title=Chile Stocks Surge as Communist Knocked Out of Presidential Race|website=Bloomberg|date=20 July 2021|orig-date=First published 18 July 2021|access-date=20 July 2021|archive-date=19 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210719200859/https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-07-18/chile-holds-key-primary-vote-in-wide-open-presidential-race|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 17 March 2021, Boric's party, [[Social Convergence]], proclaimed him as its presidential candidate.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.24horas.cl/politica/gabriel-boric-carta-presidencial-4696569|title=Convergencia Social proclama a diputado Gabriel Boric como su carta presidencial|website=24 Horas|date=17 March 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=23 March 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210323025308/https://www.24horas.cl/politica/gabriel-boric-carta-presidencial-4696569|url-status=live}}</ref> The [[Commons (Chilean political party)|Commons]] Party's leadership also announced on 17 March 2021 that it would propose Boric as its presidential candidate in a meeting of the party's leadership the following Saturday.<ref>{{cite web|last=Caro|first=Isabel|url=https://www.latercera.com/la-tercera-pm/noticia/boric-presidenciable-directiva-de-comunes-llama-a-proclamarlo-antes-del-11-de-abril-y-a-ampliar-alianzas/5UCPQNXUERE7NKB6EMYAF5WRPQ/|title=Boric presidenciable: Directiva de Comunes llama a proclamarlo antes del 11 de abril y a ampliar alianzas|website=La Tercera|date=17 March 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=3 August 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210803234354/https://www.latercera.com/la-tercera-pm/noticia/boric-presidenciable-directiva-de-comunes-llama-a-proclamarlo-antes-del-11-de-abril-y-a-ampliar-alianzas/5UCPQNXUERE7NKB6EMYAF5WRPQ/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 23 March 2021, [[Democratic Revolution]], the coalition's largest party, proclaimed Boric as its presidential candidate.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2021/03/23/1015780/RD-proclama-Boric-candidato-presidencial.html|title=Consejo Político de RD decide proclamar a Gabriel Boric como su candidato presidencial &#124; Emol.com|first=B.|last=Osses|date=23 March 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|website=Emol|language=es-CL|archive-date=20 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211220201550/https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2021/03/23/1015780/RD-proclama-Boric-candidato-presidencial.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On 29 May 2021, the [[Common Force]] movement gave its support to Boric, after he beat Marcelo Díaz in a plebiscite held on May 27–28.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.elperiodista.cl/2021/03/fuerza-comun-concreta-apoyo-presidencial-a-gabriel-boric-como-abanderado-del-frente-amplio/|title=Fuerza Común concreta apoyo presidencial a Gabriel Boric como abanderado del Frente Amplio|website=El Periodista|date=29 March 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=22 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210522002939/https://www.elperiodista.cl/2021/03/fuerza-comun-concreta-apoyo-presidencial-a-gabriel-boric-como-abanderado-del-frente-amplio/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 17 August 2021, the Acción Humanista movement proclaimed him as its candidate.<ref>{{Cite news|title=Acción Humanista proclama a Gabriel Boric como candidato presidencial|url=https://www.cnnchile.com/pais/accion-humanista-gabriel-boric-candidato-presidencial_20210817/|date=17 August 2021|access-date=23 August 2021|work=CNN Chile|language=es-CL|archive-date=23 August 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210823145041/https://www.cnnchile.com/pais/accion-humanista-gabriel-boric-candidato-presidencial_20210817/|url-status=live}}</ref>

====Defeated in primary====
{{Main|2021 Chilean presidential primaries}}

*'''[[Daniel Jadue]]''' ([[Communist Party of Chile|PC]]): Jadue is the mayor of [[Recoleta, Chile|Recoleta]] and a member of the Communist Party of Chile. He studied sociology at the [[University of Chile]], and also studied [[total quality management]] at the [[Catholic University of the North]].<ref>{{cite web|date=29 October 2020|title=Daniel Jadue – Daniel Jadue|url=https://www.danieljadue.cl/web/acerca-de/|access-date=10 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201029134717/https://www.danieljadue.cl/web/acerca-de/|archive-date=29 October 2020}}</ref> He appeared as the candidate with the most support in several opinion polls.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tuinfluyes.com/assets/estudios/ESTUDIO_TUINFLUYES_OCTUBRE_2020.pdf|title=Post Plebiscito, Constituyentes, Presidenciales y Gobierno - Estudio Cuantitativo|website=TúInfluyes|date=October 2020|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=11 November 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211111152450/https://www.tuinfluyes.com/assets/estudios/ESTUDIO_TUINFLUYES_OCTUBRE_2020.pdf|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Barómetro del trabajo|url=https://fielchile.cl/v2/barometro-del-trabajo/|website=Fundación Instituto de Estudios Laborales|access-date=14 February 2021|language=es|archive-date=26 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210226185656/https://fielchile.cl/v2/barometro-del-trabajo/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.criteria.cl/descargas/Agenda_Criteria_Agosto_2020_6y7fw.pdf|title=Agenda Criteria Agosto 2020|website=Criteria Chile|date=August 2020|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=20 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211220201543/https://www.criteria.cl/descargas/Agenda_Criteria_Agosto_2020_6y7fw.pdf|url-status=live}}</ref>

====Dropped out====

*'''[[Marcelo Díaz Díaz|Marcelo Díaz]]''' ([[Unir Movement|Unir]]): In November 2020 the [[Unir Movement]] presented the deputy and former spokesman as pre-candidate.<ref name="auto1">{{cite web|last=Garrido|first=Mónica|url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/carrera-por-la-moneda-asi-quedo-el-abanico-presidencial-en-la-oposicion-tras-la-irrupcion-de-gabriel-boric/IZO7YE5Y2JHSDOG5JPJRCQUCHA/|title=Carrera por la Moneda: Así quedó el abanico presidencial en la oposición tras la irrupción de Gabriel Boric|website=La Tercera|date=18 March 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=22 March 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210322013131/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/carrera-por-la-moneda-asi-quedo-el-abanico-presidencial-en-la-oposicion-tras-la-irrupcion-de-gabriel-boric/IZO7YE5Y2JHSDOG5JPJRCQUCHA/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 18 May 2021 he dropped out of the race and lent his support to Boric.<ref>{{cite web|last1=Jara|first1=Alejandra|last2=Cáceres|first2=Felipe|last3=Garrido|first3=Mónica|url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/marcelo-diaz-baja-candidatura-presidencial-y-anuncia-apoyo-a-boric-estoy-convencido-que-es-posible-que-el-fa-lidere-el-proximo-gobierno/VJFABXEBJRGBXAFBAEBOR6HLVQ/|title=Marcelo Díaz baja candidatura presidencial y anuncia apoyo a Boric: "Estoy convencido de que es posible que el FA lidere el próximo gobierno"|date=18 May 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|website=La Tercera|language=es-CL|archive-date=19 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210519174844/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/marcelo-diaz-baja-candidatura-presidencial-y-anuncia-apoyo-a-boric-estoy-convencido-que-es-posible-que-el-fa-lidere-el-proximo-gobierno/VJFABXEBJRGBXAFBAEBOR6HLVQ/|url-status=live}}</ref>
*'''[[Jaime Mulet]]''' ([[Social Green Regionalist Federation|FRVS]]): The current president of the FRVS and deputy was proclaimed as his party's presidential candidate in September 2020.<ref name="auto1" /> In May 2021, he received the support of the Christian Left movement.<ref>{{cite web|date=12 May 2021|title="Izquierda Cristiana se suma a la candidatura presidencial de Jaime Mulet y a trabajar por la unidad para todos los procesos venideros"|url=https://www.cronicadigital.cl/2021/05/12/izquierda-cristiana-se-suma-ala-candidatura-presidencial-de-jaime-mulet-y-a-trabajar-por-la-unidad-para-todos-los-procesos-venideros/|access-date=20 July 2021|website=Crónica Digital|language=es-CL|archive-date=19 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210719085543/https://www.cronicadigital.cl/2021/05/12/izquierda-cristiana-se-suma-ala-candidatura-presidencial-de-jaime-mulet-y-a-trabajar-por-la-unidad-para-todos-los-procesos-venideros/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 8 July 2021, the FRVS chose to support the candidacy of Daniel Jadue.<ref>{{cite web|date=8 July 2021|title=FRVS oficializa apoyo a candidatura de Daniel Jadue en elecciones primarias|url=https://radio.uchile.cl/2021/07/08/frvs-oficializa-apoyo-a-candidatura-de-daniel-jadue-en-elecciones-primarias/|access-date=20 July 2021|website=Diario y Radio U Chile|language=es-CL|archive-date=19 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210719184609/https://radio.uchile.cl/2021/07/08/frvs-oficializa-apoyo-a-candidatura-de-daniel-jadue-en-elecciones-primarias/|url-status=live}}</ref>
{{Clear}}

===Chile Podemos Más===
{| class="wikitable" style="float:right; font-size:90%; text-align:center; margin:10px;"
|-
| style="background:#f1f1f1;" |[[File:Chile Podemos +.svg|150x120px|center]] '''{{lang|es|italic=no|[[Chile Vamos|Chile Podemos Más]]}}'''
|-
! style="font-size:120%; background:gold; width:200px;"|{{colored link|black|Sebastián Sichel}}<br /><small>{{colored link|black|Independent politician|(Independent)}}</small>
|-
| [[File:SEBASTIAN SICHEL 2019.jpg|center|200x200px|border]]
|-
| [[Ministry of Social Development (Chile)|Minister of Social Development]]<br /><small>(2019-2020)</small>
|}
The {{lang|es|italic=no|[[Chile Vamos|Chile Podemos Más]]}} center-right coalition (previously {{lang|es|italic=no|Chile Vamos}}) participated in the publicly-funded primaries held nationwide on 18 July 2021.<ref>{{cite web|url = https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/chile-vamos-inscribe-primarias-presidenciales-ante-el-servel-y-define-orden-de-sus-candidatos-en-la-papeleta-para-el-18-de-julio/B4VYNOJ7XNAUBKZBYWZSNHBPCU/|title = Chile Vamos inscribe primarias presidenciales ante el Servel y define orden de sus candidatos en la papeleta para el 18 de julio|website = La Tercera|date = 19 May 2021|access-date = 14 July 2021|language = es-CL|archive-date = 2 June 2021|archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210602214424/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/chile-vamos-inscribe-primarias-presidenciales-ante-el-servel-y-define-orden-de-sus-candidatos-en-la-papeleta-para-el-18-de-julio/B4VYNOJ7XNAUBKZBYWZSNHBPCU/|url-status = live}}</ref> Former minister [[Sebastián Sichel]] beat the other three candidates by 49% of the vote.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/mundo/noticias-america-latina-57883422|title=Elecciones en Chile: Gabriel Boric y Sebastián Sichel ganan las primarias y son los dos primeros candidatos que buscarán la presidencia en las elecciones de noviembre|date=18 July 2021|access-date=19 July 2021|website=BBC Mundo|language=es-CL|archive-date=19 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210719001220/https://www.bbc.com/mundo/noticias-america-latina-57883422|url-status=live}}</ref>

Sichel was minister of Social Development and president of [[Banco del Estado de Chile|BancoEstado]] during the second administration of President [[Sebastián Piñera]]. He participated as an independent candidate in the {{lang|es|italic=no|Chile Podemos Más}} primary, supported by former [[Christian Democratic Party (Chile)|PDC]] supporters and other centrist political movements.<ref>{{cite web|title=Sichel: "Soy candidato a presidente como independiente en la primaria de Chile Vamos"|url=https://www.cnnchile.com/pais/sebastian-sichel-candidato-independiente-primaria-chiela-vamos_20201220/|access-date=14 February 2021|website=CNN Chile|language=es|archive-date=7 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210207052030/https://www.cnnchile.com/pais/sebastian-sichel-candidato-independiente-primaria-chiela-vamos_20201220/|url-status=live}}</ref>

====Defeated in primary====
{{Main|2021 Chilean presidential primaries}}
*'''[[Ignacio Briones]]''' ([[Political Evolution|Evópoli]]): Briones is a university professor and economist who served as minister of Finance between 2019 and 2021. He was unanimously proclaimed by the [[Evópoli|Political Evolution]] party as their presidential candidate on 30 January 2021.<ref>{{cite web|date=30 January 2021|title=Evópoli proclama de forma unánime a Ignacio Briones como su precandidato presidencial|url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2021/01/30/1010839/Evopoli-Ignacio-Briones-candidato-presidencial.html|access-date=14 February 2021|website=Emol|language=Spanish|archive-date=20 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211220201545/https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2021/01/30/1010839/Evopoli-Ignacio-Briones-candidato-presidencial.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He describes himself as a [[social liberalism|social liberal]] and seeks to promote liberal policies, although he is against abortion.
*'''[[Mario Desbordes]]''' ([[National Renewal (Chile)|RN]]): Desbordes became minister of Defense in July 2020. Before that, he was a member of the [[Chamber of Deputies of Chile|Chamber of Deputies]]. He was also president of his party between 2018 and 2020 and secretary-general between 2010 and 2018. During the first administration of President [[Sebastián Piñera]], he had a stint as undersecretary of Investigations. He was proclaimed by the [[Independent Regionalist Party|PRI]] party as their candidate on 29 December 2020.<ref>{{cite web|date=29 December 2020|title=PRI proclama a Mario Desbordes como su candidato presidencial para la primaria de Chile Vamos|url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2020/12/29/1007936/PRI-proclama-a-Desbordes.html|access-date=14 February 2021|website=Emol|language=es|archive-date=20 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211220201555/https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2020/12/29/1007936/PRI-proclama-a-Desbordes.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On 23 January 2021 his own party, RN, chose him as their contender for the {{lang|es|italic=no|Chile Vamos}} primary race after winning nearly 73% of the vote of the General Council.<ref>{{cite web|title=RN proclama a Mario Desbordes como su candidato presidencial|url=https://www.pauta.cl/politica/consejo-general-de-rn-proclama-a-mario-desbordes-como-presidenciable|access-date=14 February 2021|website=pauta|language=es-CL|archive-date=1 March 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210301044134/https://www.pauta.cl/politica/consejo-general-de-rn-proclama-a-mario-desbordes-como-presidenciable|url-status=live}}</ref>
*'''[[Joaquín Lavín]]''' ([[Independent Democratic Union|UDI]]): Lavín studied economics at the [[University of Chicago]]. He was a presidential candidate in the [[1999-2000 Chilean presidential election|1999]] and [[2005-06 Chilean presidential election|2005]] elections. He was also an economic appraiser of the [[Neoliberalism|neoliberal]] policies of Chile's [[Military dictatorship of Chile (1973–1990)|military dictatorship]]. As mayor of [[Las Condes]] he actively promoted social housing programs for the poor and social integration with the rest of the cities, as well as enlarged use of technology in law enforcement and moderate social policies.<ref>{{cite web|title=Primer enfrentamiento entre vecinos por edificio social en Las Condes|url=https://www.chvnoticias.cl/trending/primer-enfrentamiento-entre-vecinos-por-edificio-social-en-las-condes_20180710/|access-date=10 December 2020|website=CHV Noticias|language=es|archive-date=20 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211220201549/https://www.chvnoticias.cl/nacional/primer-enfrentamiento-entre-vecinos-por-edificio-social-en-las-condes_20180710/|url-status=live}}</ref> He appeared as the candidate with the most support in most opinion polls.<ref name="activa">{{cite web|date=November 2020|title=PULSO CIUDADANO Noviembre 2020/ Primera Quincena (12 al 14 de Noviembre)|url=https://chile.activasite.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Pulso_ciudadano_NOVIEMBRE_Q1.pdf|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210714070719/https://chile.activasite.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Pulso_ciudadano_NOVIEMBRE_Q1.pdf|archive-date=14 July 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|website=|language=es-CL}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Encuesta Plaza Pública - Segunda semana de Noviembre - Estudio N°357|url=https://plazapublica.cl/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Track-PP-357-Noviembre-S2.pdf|website=Plaza Pública Cadem|date=November 2020|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=11 November 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211111152451/https://plazapublica.cl/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Track-PP-357-Noviembre-S2.pdf|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=October 2020|title=PULSO CIUDADANO Octubre 2020/ Segunda Quincena (29 al 31 de Octubre)|url=https://chile.activasite.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Pulso_ciudadano_OCTUBRE_Q2.pdf|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210714070723/https://chile.activasite.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/Pulso_ciudadano_OCTUBRE_Q2.pdf|archive-date=14 July 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|website=|language=es-CL}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=September 2020|title=PULSO CIUDADANO Septiembre 2020/ Segunda Quincena (25 al 28 de Septiembre)|url=https://chile.activasite.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Pulso-Ciudadano-Septiembre-Q2.pdf|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210714070728/https://chile.activasite.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Pulso-Ciudadano-Septiembre-Q2.pdf|archive-date=14 July 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|website=|language=es-CL}}</ref>

====Did not run====

*'''[[Evelyn Matthei]]''' ([[Independent Democratic Union|UDI]]): Matthei is a right-wing politician. She studied at the [[Pontifical Catholic University of Chile]]. In 1993 she was the target of a [[Piñeragate|scheme]] by Sebastián Piñera to prevent her from becoming a candidate for the presidency that year.<ref>{{cite web|date=11 May 2012|title=La Tercera - El caso Piñeragate y la bomba que dejó caer Ricardo Claro sobre RN|url=http://www.latercera.cl/contenido/23_67488_9.shtml|website=La Tercera|access-date=10 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120511071312/http://www.latercera.cl/contenido/23_67488_9.shtml|archive-date=11 May 2012|language=es-CL}}</ref> She was a senator<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.latercera.com/noticia/politica/2013/07/674-533523-9-nueve-claves-que-han-marcado-la-carrera-politica-de-evelyn-matthei.shtml|title=Nueve hechos que han marcado la carrera política de Evelyn Matthei &#124; Política &#124; LA TERCERA|date=20 July 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130720212600/https://www.latercera.com/noticia/politica/2013/07/674-533523-9-nueve-claves-que-han-marcado-la-carrera-politica-de-evelyn-matthei.shtml|website=La Tercera|archive-date=20 July 2013|language=es-CL}}</ref> and candidate in [[2013 Chilean general election|Chile's presidential elections in 2013]], losing to [[Michelle Bachelet]], the [[Socialist Party of Chile|Socialist]] candidate. She dropped out of the race on 17 May 2021, a day after being re-elected as mayor of [[Providencia, Chile|Providencia]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pauta.cl/politica/evelyn-matthei-se-baja-de-la-carrera-presidencial|title=Evelyn Matthei se baja de la carrera presidencial|last=Bobadilla|first=Matías|date=17 May 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|website=pauta|language=es-CL|archive-date=2 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602220028/https://www.pauta.cl/politica/evelyn-matthei-se-baja-de-la-carrera-presidencial|url-status=live}}</ref>

===New Social Pact===
{| class="wikitable" style="float:right; font-size:90%; text-align:center; margin:10px;"
|-
| style="background:#f1f1f1;" |[[File:Nuevo Pacto Social full.png|150x120px|center]] '''[[Constituent Unity|New Social Pact]]'''
|-
! style=" font-size:120%; background:purple; width:200px;"|{{colored link|white|Yasna Provoste}}<br /><small>{{colored link|white|Christian Democratic Party (Chile)|(Christian Democratic Party)}}</small>
