| [[Senate of Chile|Senator]] for [[Atacama Region|Atacama]]<br /><small>(since 2018)</small><br /> [[President of the Senate of Chile|President of the Senate]]<br /><small>(2021)</small>
|}
[[Christian Democratic Party (Chile)|Christian Democrat]] Senator [[Yasna Provoste]] won the primary election held by the [[Constituent Unity|New Social Pact]] center-left coalition (formerly Constituent Unity) on August 21, 2021, with over 60% of the vote and a turnout of around 150,000.<ref>{{Cite news |date=21 August 2021 |title=Con escasa participación, Provoste (DC) se convierte en la abanderada de Unidad Constituyente |language=es-CL |work=La Tercera |url=https://www.latercera.com/la-tercera-domingo/noticia/con-escasa-participacion-provoste-dc-se-convierte-en-la-abanderada-de-unidad-constituyente/I4CHJ6BPIRCLVL7BTM5WN2SYI4/ |url-status=live |access-date=23 August 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210823002506/https://www.latercera.com/la-tercera-domingo/noticia/con-escasa-participacion-provoste-dc-se-convierte-en-la-abanderada-de-unidad-constituyente/I4CHJ6BPIRCLVL7BTM5WN2SYI4/ |archive-date=23 August 2021}}</ref> On May 30, 2021, Provoste had expressed her willingness to compete if her party deemed it necessary.<ref>{{cite web |last=Dote |first=Sebastián |date=30 May 2021 |title=Yasna Provoste: "Estaré disponible para lo que la DC estime que sea necesario" |url=https://www.eldinamo.cl/politica/2021/05/30/yasna-provoste-estare-disponible-para-lo-que-la-dc-estime-que-sea-necesario/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210608071816/https://www.eldinamo.cl/politica/2021/05/30/yasna-provoste-estare-disponible-para-lo-que-la-dc-estime-que-sea-necesario/ |archive-date=8 June 2021 |access-date=14 July 2021 |website=El Dínamo |language=es-CL}}</ref> She officially launched her candidacy on July 23, 2021, during a ceremony in her hometown of [[Vallenar]], in northern Chile. On August 17, 2021, the Christian Democratic Party proclaimed her as their candidate.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Cáceres |first=Felipe |date=17 August 2021 |title=Junta nacional DC proclama formalmente a Yasna Provoste como su candidata presidencial |language=es-CL |work=La Tercera |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/junta-nacional-dc-proclama-formalmente-a-yasna-provoste-como-su-candidata-presidencial/FEZFMT2FX5B45GZAXR6MAFLXM4/ |url-status=live |access-date=23 August 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210823144606/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/junta-nacional-dc-proclama-formalmente-a-yasna-provoste-como-su-candidata-presidencial/FEZFMT2FX5B45GZAXR6MAFLXM4/ |archive-date=23 August 2021}}</ref>

The other primary candidates, Paula Narváez and Carlos Maldonado, urged the need for a primary to determine a single candidate<ref>{{cite web |last=Reyes P. |first=Carlos |date=19 July 2021 |title=Narváez urge a la Unidad Constituyente y al progresismo a establecer candidatura única: "No hay más tiempo para estas definiciones y temo que de no tomarlas, el proceso sea irreversible" |url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/narvaez-urge-a-la-unidad-constituyente-y-al-progresismo-a-establecer-candidatura-unica-no-hay-mas-tiempo-para-estas-definiciones-y-temo-que-de-no-tomarlas-el-proceso-sea-irreversible/2P6ZVMJ7Y5ARZBQAEJ4WWZPCYU/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210719214648/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/narvaez-urge-a-la-unidad-constituyente-y-al-progresismo-a-establecer-candidatura-unica-no-hay-mas-tiempo-para-estas-definiciones-y-temo-que-de-no-tomarlas-el-proceso-sea-irreversible/2P6ZVMJ7Y5ARZBQAEJ4WWZPCYU/ |archive-date=19 July 2021 |access-date=20 July 2021 |website=La Tercera |language=es-CL}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=17 July 2021 |title=Carlos Maldonado insiste en primarias ciudadanas de Unidad Constituyente: "Es mucho mejor que una nominación entre cuatro paredes" |url=https://www.eldesconcierto.cl/nacional/2021/07/17/carlos-maldonado-insiste-en-primarias-ciudadanas-de-unidad-constituyente-es-mucho-mejor-que-una-nominacion-entre-cuatro-paredes.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210720050121/https://www.eldesconcierto.cl/nacional/2021/07/17/carlos-maldonado-insiste-en-primarias-ciudadanas-de-unidad-constituyente-es-mucho-mejor-que-una-nominacion-entre-cuatro-paredes.html |archive-date=20 July 2021 |access-date=20 July 2021 |website=El Desconcierto |language=es-CL}}</ref> after the coalition failed to come to an agreement to participate in the national publicly-funded primaries held on July 18, 2021.<ref>{{cite web |date=19 May 2021 |title=Partido Socialista resuelve no inscribir a Paula Narváez a primarias con el PC y el Frente Amplio |url=https://www.t13.cl/noticia/elecciones-2021/politica/partido-socialista-resuelve-no-inscribir-paula-narvaez-primarias-unidad-constituyente |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210712041701/https://www.t13.cl/noticia/elecciones-2021/politica/partido-socialista-resuelve-no-inscribir-paula-narvaez-primarias-unidad-constituyente |archive-date=12 July 2021 |access-date=14 July 2021 |website=Tele13 |language=es-CL}}</ref> 

==== Defeated in primary ====
*'''[[Carlos Maldonado Curti|Carlos Maldonado]]''' ([[Radical Party (Chile)|PR]]): The former minister of Justice and current president of the [[Radical Party (Chile)|Radical Party]] was proclaimed as presidential candidate on 23 December 2020.<ref>{{cite web|last=Osses|first=B.|date=23 December 2020|title=Consejo General del PR proclama a Maldonado como candidato presidencial: "Asumo esta responsabilidad con convicción" {{!}} Emol.com|url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2020/12/23/1007423/PR-Carlos-Maldonado-candidato-presidencial.html|access-date=14 February 2021|website=Emol|language=Spanish|archive-date=20 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211220203516/https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2020/12/23/1007423/PR-Carlos-Maldonado-candidato-presidencial.html|url-status=live}}</ref> On 20 May 2021 he announced he would go straight to the November election.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.t13.cl/noticia/elecciones-2021/politica/carlos-maldonado-asegura-llegara-primera-vuelta-presidencial-20-05-21|title=Carlos Maldonado asegura que llegará a primera vuelta y dice que "faltó voluntad" por primarias|website=Tele13|language=Spanish|date=2021-05-20|access-date=2 June 2021|archive-date=21 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210521111900/https://www.t13.cl/noticia/elecciones-2021/politica/carlos-maldonado-asegura-llegara-primera-vuelta-presidencial-20-05-21|url-status=live}}</ref> On July 3, 2021, he backtracked on his decision and declared himself available to compete in a possible coalition primary.<ref>{{cite web|last=Vallejos|first=Leonardo|url=https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2021/07/03/1025639/maldonado-pr-primaria-centroizquierda.html|title=Carlos Maldonado se retracta y ahora confirma intención de ir a primaria convencional de la centroizquierda|website=Emol|date=3 July 2021|language=es-CL|access-date=19 July 2021|archive-date=20 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211220203519/https://www.emol.com/noticias/Nacional/2021/07/03/1025639/maldonado-pr-primaria-centroizquierda.html|url-status=live}}</ref>
*'''[[Paula Narváez]]''' ([[Socialist Party of Chile|PS]]): The former minister was proclaimed by the [[Socialist Party of Chile|Socialist Party]]'s Central Committee as its presidential candidate on 28 January 2021 in a unanimous vote.<ref>{{cite web|last=Reyes P.|first=Carlos|date=28 January 2021|title=Partido Socialista proclama de forma unánime a Paula Narváez como su candidata presidencial: "Sé que estaremos a la altura del desafío de este nuevo Chile que emerge"|url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/partido-socialista-proclama-a-paula-narvaez-como-su-candidata-presidencial-se-que-estaremos-a-la-altura-del-desafio-de-este-nuevo-chile-que-emerge/76MLYGRB45BFZKTFTM3TKNIODQ/|access-date=14 February 2021|website=La Tercera|language=es-CL|archive-date=29 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210129212000/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/partido-socialista-proclama-a-paula-narvaez-como-su-candidata-presidencial-se-que-estaremos-a-la-altura-del-desafio-de-este-nuevo-chile-que-emerge/76MLYGRB45BFZKTFTM3TKNIODQ/|url-status=live}}</ref> Her candidacy emerged after a December 2020 [[Change.org]] petition made by female members of the PS asking Narváez to become the party's candidate was signed by former president [[Michelle Bachelet]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Con la venia de Bachelet: ¿Cómo Paula Narváez mueve las aguas presidenciales en el PS?|url=https://www.pauta.cl/politica/con-la-venia-de-bachelet-como-paula-narvaez-mueve-las-aguas|access-date=14 February 2021|website=pauta|language=es-CL|archive-date=7 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210207110901/https://www.pauta.cl/politica/con-la-venia-de-bachelet-como-paula-narvaez-mueve-las-aguas|url-status=live}}</ref> In January 2021 both senator [[José Miguel Insulza]] and PS president [[Álvaro Elizalde]] dropped out of the race.<ref>{{cite web|date=16 January 2021|title=Vía libre para Narváez en el PS: Insulza asume cuota de realidad y se baja de la carrera presidencial|url=https://www.elmostrador.cl/destacado/2021/01/16/via-libre-para-narvaez-en-el-ps-insulza-asume-cuota-de-realidad-y-se-baja-de-la-carrera-presidencial/|access-date=14 February 2021|website=El Mostrador|language=es|archive-date=7 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210207124603/https://www.elmostrador.cl/destacado/2021/01/16/via-libre-para-narvaez-en-el-ps-insulza-asume-cuota-de-realidad-y-se-baja-de-la-carrera-presidencial/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 5 June 2021 the PPD officially proclaimed her as its candidate.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/ppd-proclama-a-paula-narvaez-como-su-candidata-presidencial-lo-vemos-como-un-paso-muy-importante-para-unir-al-socialismo-democratico/Z336GHTXDBGG7PNS4AY63OAKHQ/|title=PPD proclama a Paula Narváez como su candidata presidencial: "Lo vemos como un paso muy importante para unir al socialismo democrático"|first=Claudia|last=Cornejo|date=5 June 2021|website=La Tercera|language=es-CL|access-date=5 June 2021|archive-date=5 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210605202932/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/ppd-proclama-a-paula-narvaez-como-su-candidata-presidencial-lo-vemos-como-un-paso-muy-importante-para-unir-al-socialismo-democratico/Z336GHTXDBGG7PNS4AY63OAKHQ/|url-status=live}}</ref>

====Dropped out====

*'''[[Heraldo Muñoz]]''' ([[Party for Democracy (Chile)|PPD]]): The current president of the [[Party for Democracy (Chile)|PPD]] and former [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Chile)|minister of Foreign Affairs]] became the PPD candidate after beating former [[Ministry of the Interior and Public Security (Chile)|minister of Interior]] and [[Ministry General Secretariat of Government (Chile)|spokesperson]] [[Francisco Vidal Salinas|Francisco Vidal]] and former deputy for District 39 and ambassador [[Jorge Tarud]] by 54% of the vote in a primary held on 31 January 2021.<ref>{{cite web|last=Minay|first=Sebastián|date=1 February 2021|title=Heraldo Muñoz vence a Vidal en primarias presidenciales del PPD luego de conflictivo proceso|url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/heraldo-munoz-vence-a-vidal-en-primarias-presidenciales-del-ppd-luego-de-conflictivo-proceso/2WOSTEFGGFCHRA27ZDWBOYEO2Q/|access-date=14 February 2021|website=La Tercera|language=es-CL|archive-date=5 February 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210205172250/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/heraldo-munoz-vence-a-vidal-en-primarias-presidenciales-del-ppd-luego-de-conflictivo-proceso/2WOSTEFGGFCHRA27ZDWBOYEO2Q/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 19 May 2021 he dropped out of the race and lent his support to Narváez.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.elmostrador.cl/dia/2021/05/19/heraldo-munoz-se-baja-de-la-carrera-presidencial-y-entrega-apoyo-a-paula-narvaez-su-candidatura-ahora-es-la-nuestra/|title=Heraldo Muñoz se baja de la carrera presidencial y entrega apoyo a Paula Narváez: "Su candidatura ahora es la nuestra"|website=El Mostrador|date=19 May 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=20 December 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211220203521/https://www.elmostrador.cl/dia/2021/05/19/heraldo-munoz-se-baja-de-la-carrera-presidencial-y-entrega-apoyo-a-paula-narvaez-su-candidatura-ahora-es-la-nuestra/|url-status=live}}</ref>
*'''[[Ximena Rincón]]''' ([[Christian Democratic Party (Chile)|PDC]]): The current senator was proclaimed as the [[Christian Democratic Party (Chile)|Christian Democratic Party]]'s candidate for president after she beat former mayor and minister [[Alberto Undurraga]] in a primary held on 24 January 2021. She won by 57% of the vote.<ref>{{cite web|title=Ximena Rincón gana las primarias presidenciales DC|url=https://www.pauta.cl/politica/ximena-rincon-primarias-presidenciales-dc-triunfo|access-date=14 February 2021|website=pauta|language=es-CL|archive-date=26 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210126043746/https://www.pauta.cl/politica/ximena-rincon-primarias-presidenciales-dc-triunfo|url-status=live}}</ref> She officially dropped out of the race on 2 June 2021.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.publimetro.cl/cl/noticias/2021/06/02/ximena-rincon-candidata.html|title=Ximena Rincón se baja definitivamente de la carrera presidencial: "No seré candidata"|website=Publimetro|date=2 June 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=2 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602234738/https://www.publimetro.cl/cl/noticias/2021/06/02/ximena-rincon-candidata.html|url-status=live}}</ref>
*'''[[Pablo Vidal]]''' ([[independent politician]]): The deputy quit the [[Democratic Revolution]] party in December 2020 and founded the New Deal ({{lang|es|Nuevo Trato}}) political platform.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://radio.uchile.cl/2020/12/03/diputados-pablo-vidal-y-natalia-castillo-renuncian-a-rd-acusando-izquierdizacion-de-la-colectividad/|title=Diputados Pablo Vidal y Natalia Castillo renuncian a RD acusando izquierdización de la colectividad « Diario y Radio U Chile|website=Diario y Radio [[University of Chile|U Chile]]|date=3 December 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=1 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210601185758/https://radio.uchile.cl/2020/12/03/diputados-pablo-vidal-y-natalia-castillo-renuncian-a-rd-acusando-izquierdizacion-de-la-colectividad/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 13 April 2021, he was proclaimed as presidential candidate by the [[Liberal Party of Chile (2013)|Liberal Party]] and New Deal.<ref>{{cite web|last=Jara|first=Alejandra|url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/partido-liberal-y-nuevo-trato-proclaman-a-pablo-vidal-como-su-candidato-presidencial/L2YA4ABCKJCF3K42O5TPQ5XSLE/|title=Partido Liberal y Nuevo Trato proclaman a Pablo Vidal como su candidato presidencial|website=La Tercera|date=14 April 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=13 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210513065334/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/partido-liberal-y-nuevo-trato-proclaman-a-pablo-vidal-como-su-candidato-presidencial/L2YA4ABCKJCF3K42O5TPQ5XSLE/|url-status=live}}</ref> On 19 May 2021 he dropped out of the race and lent his support to Narváez.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.elmostrador.cl/dia/2021/05/19/nuevo-trato-baja-candidatura-de-pablo-vidal-y-entrega-apoyo-a-la-postulante-del-ps-paula-narvaez/|title=Nuevo Trato baja candidatura de Pablo Vidal y entrega apoyo a la postulante del PS Paula Narváez|website=El Mostrador|date=19 May 2021|access-date=14 July 2021|language=es-CL|archive-date=6 June 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210606152402/https://www.elmostrador.cl/dia/2021/05/19/nuevo-trato-baja-candidatura-de-pablo-vidal-y-entrega-apoyo-a-la-postulante-del-ps-paula-narvaez/|url-status=live}}</ref>

